1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,307
The bell rang three times from the empty
pier. Jason thought their contact

2
00:00:05,307 --> 00:00:06,940
had finally arrived tonight.

3
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:11,431
Lucia saw nobody behind the visitor
counter, only an empty satchel

4
00:00:11,431 --> 00:00:13,880
somebody had carefully placed beneath
it.

5
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:18,772
A handwritten sign promised payment for
bringing that bag to a waiting

6
00:00:18,772 --> 00:00:20,810
truck beyond the mangrove bend.

7
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:26,117
Jason lifted the strap. The bell rang
again, although both his hands were

8
00:00:26,117 --> 00:00:27,750
right there in sight.

9
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:31,832
Lucia followed the sound upward.
Rainwater filled a broken gutter,

10
00:00:31,832 --> 00:00:34,690
tipping a loose board against the bell.

11
00:00:34,690 --> 00:00:39,582
They had spent an hour answering
weather. Their contact had never come.

12
00:00:39,582 --> 00:00:41,620
Neither had the promised money.

13
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:46,519
Jason put the satchel back. Lucia tore
down the sign before another

14
00:00:46,519 --> 00:00:48,560
desperate stranger could believe it.

15
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:54,687
As they left, the bell rang once more.
This time, neither of them turned

16
00:00:54,687 --> 00:00:56,000
around to answer.
